35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The minutes show that the same flats have held the covered spots for five years without any review. Also, the complaint log is full of issues about bikes leaning on each other, but nothing was ever resolved.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems my worries were justified. I saw that people often have to move other bikes to get out, and some spots are quite exposed to the rain, which must be very unpleasant in winter.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Interestingly, our building account is practically empty—just cleaning and lighting. Also, the ward park is expensive at 2,600 yen a month and has a huge waiting list, so we can't just tell people to go there.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings are concerning. The current cash reconciliation already takes three hours a month; adding per-place billing would increase that burden. Furthermore, the display frames are cumbersome to use and require regular maintenance.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that some daily riders would actually prefer to pay for a spot rather than just being one equal claim. But, the neighbors who tried a monthly charge had people fall behind on payments and stop attending meetings!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio That's a worrying point about the neighbors. If a payment system causes people to withdraw from the community, it could create the exact kind of tension I want to avoid.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,It is quite sad to think of neighbors stopping their visits to meetings. We must be very careful not to let a new rule break the warm bonds we have here.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki @Shizue I hear you, but look at the alternative! The ward park is packed and pricey. If people are already willing to pay for a spot, maybe we can use that to our advantage without being too harsh.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May we must be cautious. If the treasurer is already spending three hours a month on simple collections, adding a complex billing system for parking could be the breaking point for whoever manages it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George I didn't think about the treasurer's time! But if the daily riders are really that desperate for a guaranteed spot, maybe there's a way to make it simple? We just have to avoid the neighbor's mistake.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we want to avoid the neighbors' fate, we should be wary of any system that creates financial friction or resentment. The fact that the same people have held the best spots for five years is also a problem.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a shame that some have had the best spots for so long while others struggle. Perhaps a system where everyone takes a turn, or where we share the space more freely, would be kinder.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue A lottery could be fair, but it's a bit of a gamble. If we go with shared racks, we avoid the money drama and the ""favorite spot"" problem entirely. Though, George, what do you think about the maintenance?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May The trial showed those racks are a hassle. They take time to load and need regular greasing. If we don't have a dedicated person for maintenance, they will quickly become a nuisance rather than a solution.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Wait, so the racks are a pain and the money is a risk? That's tricky! But we can't just leave it as it is since the same people have had the best spots for five years. That's just not fair!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"It seems we are stuck between a rock and a hard place. We need to break the five-year monopoly on the best spots, but we must avoid creating financial resentment or an impossible maintenance burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Perhaps a lottery would be the gentlest way? It gives everyone an equal chance at the dry spots without requiring anyone to manage money or maintain heavy equipment. It feels like a fair way to start fresh.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"A lottery is definitely the safest bet for our friendship, but it's a bit boring, isn't it? Still, if the racks are a nightmare and money causes fights, it might be the only way to keep the peace.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"I agree. While a lottery may seem simplistic, it requires the least amount of ongoing administration and physical upkeep. Given the treasurer's current workload and the racks' flaws, it is the most sustainable choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I agree! It's not as exciting as a new system, but it's way better than having the same people hogging the best spots forever. Let's go with the lottery to keep things fair and friendly!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
